NAME
     pgrep - find, or signal, processes by name

SYNOPSIS
     pgrep [-l] [-u USER] PATTERN
     pkill [-SIGNAL] [-u USER] PATTERN
     killall [-SIGNAL] NAME

DESCRIPTION
     pgrep prints the process ids whose command matches PATTERN. Called
     as pkill or killall it signals them instead -- TERM by default.

OPTIONS
     -l          print the name beside the id
     -u USER     only that user's processes
     -SIGNAL     pkill, killall: the signal to send

SEE ALSO
     ps(1), kill(1), top(1)
